# the Arrangement page (SEL; PERFORM's that was): white 1-6 mute the parts (1.4.0, the user's: the chord, the pings,
# the bass, the kick, the hats, the noise; held, a part's strip: strips.amb); black 1-5 each the part of the white key
# on its left (the chord, the pings, the bass, the hats, the noise; the kick none): a tap a solo, held a throw (that
# part into the echo); white 7 none (the gap), white 8-11 held the global moves (Open, Shut, Drop, Echo), white 12-16
# held five of the grid's effects (Time x2, Freeze, Tape stop, Stutter, Siren); the knobs Width, (none), Wet, Duck (the
# Mix, white 6 held, gone: the levels the strips'); SEL again stays (one page); a page's button or SELECT gives the
# scale back
listen
wait 3000
expect pool 0x6AD
tap SEL
wait 200
said ARRANGEMENT ON
tapkey w3
wait 200
said KICK OFF
tapkey w0
wait 200
said CHORD OFF
# white 7: none (the gap between the parts and the moves; dark)
tapkey w6
wait 200
expect mutes 9
expect view 17
# white 8-11: the global moves, held (Open, Shut, Drop, Echo)
key w7 down
wait 200
said OPEN
wait 1000
key w7 up
key w10 down
wait 200
said ECHO
wait 1000
key w10 up
# white 12-16: the grid's effects, held (Time x2 .. Siren), alongside the grid's own
key w11 down
wait 200
said TIME X2
expect litkey19 0
expect litkey21 1
wait 800
key w11 up
key w15 down
wait 200
said SIREN
wait 800
key w15 up
# (a black key held: its part thrown; the chord's (F#3) every stab, the hats' (C#4) the hats, the rim, the clap; the
# kick never; F#4 nothing now)
key b0 down
wait 500
said CHORD THROW
wait 1500
key b0 up
wait 200
said_none SOLO
key b3 down
wait 500
said HATS THROW
expect litkey8 0
expect litkey13 0
expect litkey11 0
wait 1500
key b3 up
wait 200
said_none SOLO
key b5 down
wait 500
said_none THROW
key b5 up
wait 200
# white 6: the noise, a tap a mute (its level kept), as the others
tapkey w5
wait 200
said NOISE OFF
expect mutes 41
tapkey w5
wait 200
said NOISE ON
expect mutes 9
expect view 17
# (1.4.0) the Arrangement page's knobs: Width (the whole mix's: the user's, Energy on the Form page alone), none (the
# dub mixer's knob gone, format 30: its rides Form's Drift's, its moves the piece's), Wet, Duck (the Filter on SELECT
# only, every page's)
spin K1 -20
wait 300
said Width 20
expect par119 20
spin K1 20
wait 300
said Width 40
expect par119 40
spin K2 10
wait 300
expect par163 45
expect view 17
spin K3 27
wait 300
said Wet +50
spin K3 -25
wait 300
spin K4 52
wait 300
said Duck 100
expect par30 100
spin K4 -50
wait 300
# a black key solos its layer (the scale stays): the others go quiet; more than one play together
tapkey b0
wait 200
expect pool 0x6AD
said SOLO CHORD
tapkey b2
wait 200
said SOLO BASS
tapkey b0
wait 200
said CHORD SOLO OFF
tapkey b2
wait 200
said SOLO OFF
# (the noise's black key, D#4: its solo)
tapkey b4
wait 200
said SOLO NOISE
expect mutes 9
tapkey b4
wait 200
said SOLO OFF
tapkey w3
wait 200
said KICK ON
# (true mutes: the Drums level untouched; the chord still muted)
expect par3 80
expect mutes 1
tap SEL
wait 200
expect view 17
tap HOME
wait 200
said ARRANGEMENT OFF
# the keys are the scale again (key b0 is F#: added)
tapkey b0
wait 200
said ADDED F#
expect dirty 1
# the levels: a part's strip (its white key held: KNOB 1 its Level); SEL off goes back to the page
expect view 0
tap SEL
wait 200
expect view 17
key w1 down
wait 400
expect view 26
spin K1 -100
wait 200
expect par1 0
key w1 up
wait 200
tap HOME
wait 200
expect view 0
# keys 1-6 are true mutes, the levels kept (the strip above left Pings at 0: it stays there)
tap SEL
wait 200
tapkey w1
wait 200
expect mutes 3
expect par1 0
said PINGS OFF
tapkey w1
wait 200
expect mutes 1
expect par1 0
said PINGS ON
tapkey w0
wait 200
expect mutes 0
expect par0 52
said CHORD ON
tap HOME
# SEL held: Lock (the phrases keep their kick, groove and plan), on or off, from any page; a tap is still PERFORM
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 1
expect lock 0
press SEL
wait 700
release SEL
wait 200
said LOCK ON
expect lock 1
expect view 1
expect card 1
tap SEL
wait 200
expect view 17
tap ENV
press SEL
wait 700
release SEL
wait 200
said LOCK OFF
expect lock 0
